merge("entities/nato", 75, """
## Alleged successor to the CIA (March 2024)

In "The CIA is Being Thrown Under the Bus," Erik Carlson argued that NATO, together with the United Nations and the European Union, is becoming the Cabal's new preferred mechanism of world control, replacing the [[central-intelligence-agency|CIA]].[n] He pointed to Sweden's accession to the alliance immediately after Swedish authorities halted their investigation into the [[nord-stream-sabotage|Nord Stream pipeline explosion]] on the grounds that the case did not fall under Swedish jurisdiction, and asked whether the sequence was coincidental.[n]

Carlson's reasoning was that NATO, the UN and the EU all lie outside a returning [[donald-trump|Donald Trump]]'s control — indeed that Trump wants nothing to do with any of them — whereas Trump would have the authority to minimize or dismantle the CIA.[n] On this reading, American politicians' insistence on sending money to Ukraine is not about helping Ukraine win the war but about building up NATO, the UN and the EU: a transfer of wealth and power out of the agency and into transnational bodies.[n]

He characterized the resulting strategy as fighting America and Trump from the outside rather than from within its own government — a shift he called not a choice but a necessity, and an act of desperation that will fail miserably.[n]
""")

merge("entities/victoria-nuland", 12, """
## Retirement read as a signal (March 2024)

In "The CIA is Being Thrown Under the Bus," Erik Carlson noted that Nuland announced her retirement shortly after the story broke that the [[central-intelligence-agency|CIA]] had been operating in Ukraine since 2014.[n] He described her as the architect of the CIA overthrow of Ukraine that began in that year, and asserted that she had likely been in charge of running Ukraine's war against Russia over the preceding two years.[n]

Carlson treated the timing as part of a wider pattern in which the agency and its operatives are being exposed and abandoned as power shifts toward NATO, the United Nations and the European Union.[n] He added that when he asked his phone how long Ukraine had been at war with Russia, the [[wikipedia|Wikipedia]]-sourced answer dated the war to 2014 — a date he read as quiet corroboration of the 2014 operation.[n]
""")

merge("concepts/nord-stream-sabotage", 15, """
## Swedish investigation and NATO accession (March 2024 commentary)

Erik Carlson's "The CIA is Being Thrown Under the Bus" treats the sabotage as the point at which exposure of the [[central-intelligence-agency|CIA]] went into high gear, following reports that the agency was involved in destroying the pipeline.[n] He noted that Sweden — which had previously said it suspected an unknown state actor of responsibility — halted its probe after verifying that the case did not fall under its jurisdiction, and that Sweden joined [[nato|NATO]] immediately afterwards.[n]

Carlson asked whether that sequence was coincidental and whether NATO was becoming the Cabal's new preferred mechanism of world control in place of the agency.[n] He also cited [[vladimir-putin|Vladimir Putin]]'s interview with [[tucker-carlson|Tucker Carlson]], in which Putin accused the CIA of exactly the practices attributed to it — blowing up underwater pipelines, running color revolutions and carrying out assassinations.[n]
""")

merge("entities/mi6", 8, """
## Alleged parentage of the OSS and CIA (Carlson, 2024)

In "The CIA is Being Thrown Under the Bus," Erik Carlson described MI6 as the UK's "super spy agency," created by the [[british-cabal|British Cabal]] in 1909 alongside think tanks such as the [[tavistock-institute|Tavistock Institute]] as part of the Cabal's transition from ruling the world through its military to controlling it from the shadows.[n]

Carlson claimed that MI6 created the [[office-of-strategic-services|OSS]] in 1942, shortly after the United States entered the Second World War, expressly in order to control the US during the conflict, and that when the OSS morphed into the [[central-intelligence-agency|CIA]] in 1947 the new agency remained fully controlled by the British elites.[n] In this account MI6 and the London think tanks, rather than any American impulse, brought the United States into both world wars and presided over the creation of the [[federal-reserve|Federal Reserve]].[n]
""")

merge("entities/gina-haspel", 2, """
## Directorship in Carlson's account of Trump and the CIA

In the March 2024 article "The CIA is Being Thrown Under the Bus," Erik Carlson cited Haspel's tenure as Director of the [[central-intelligence-agency|CIA]] — taking over from [[mike-pompeo|Mike Pompeo]], who moved to Secretary of State — as the point at which [[donald-trump|Donald Trump]] stopped running intelligence through the agency.[n]

Carlson presented this as evidence that a president can contain the agency without formally dismantling it, noting that despite the CIA working against him, Trump was drawn into zero new wars during his term.[n] He suggested a returning Trump could go further and follow through on [[john-f-kennedy|John F. Kennedy]]'s stated desire to splinter the agency into a thousand pieces.[n]
""")

merge("entities/office-of-strategic-services", 5, """
## Alleged British creation and postwar continuation (Carlson, 2024)

Erik Carlson's "The CIA is Being Thrown Under the Bus" asserts that the OSS was created by [[mi6|MI6]] in 1942, shortly after the United States entered the Second World War, for the purpose of controlling the US during the conflict on behalf of the [[british-cabal|British Cabal]].[n] In 1947 the OSS is said to have morphed into the [[central-intelligence-agency|CIA]], still fully controlled by the British elites and used thereafter to enforce the Cabal's agenda.[n]

Carlson treats the decision not to dissolve the OSS after the war as the pivotal counterfactual of the twentieth century: had it been disbanded and no CIA created, he argues, the United States might have drifted out of its British handlers' control, avoided Korea, Vietnam and the later Middle Eastern wars, and sustained the postwar economic boom without the roadblocks of the 1960s and 1970s.[n] Instead, he writes, the Cabal quickly created the CIA and changed directions, thereafter controlling the world through a Cold War in which it held both sides.[n]
""")
